MANIFEST.sha256 (148 entries, written 2026-10-03T08:06:49Z by make_manifest.sh)
Hashes are SHA-256 over LF-NORMALISED content: for text files (no NUL byte) every CR byte is removed before hashing (tr -d '\r');
binary files (containing a NUL byte) are hashed raw. MANIFEST.sha256 has no comment lines, so plain 'sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256'
(or 'shasum -a 256 -c MANIFEST.sha256') works on it as is for an LF copy of the files.
For a copy with any line-ending convention (e.g. CRLF after a Windows/Drive round trip) run: verify_manifest.sh <dir>
(same normalisation; it also ignores '#' lines and CR bytes in MANIFEST.sha256 itself).
